# sweep-alias-gpu.steps -- alias models on their GPU paths through the
# SDL_GPU backend (-gpu) against GL (#340 P2e): instanced alias models
# (r_alias_gpu 1: per-frame instance storage streamed by GL_Upload, the pose
# and shadedots storage buffers, one instanced draw per model and skin) and,
# with the replacement models below, skeletal (IQM / MD5) and MD3 meshes.
#
# Run the SAME binary both ways, with identical settings:
#
#   A="-fsaa 0 +gamma 1 +map demo1"
#   STEPS=tools/sweep-alias-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/a-gl  ~/hexen2 $A
#   VK_ICD_FILENAMES=<lvp_icd json> STEPS=tools/sweep-alias-gpu.steps ENGINE=$E \
#       ./tools/headless-drive.sh script /tmp/a-gpu ~/hexen2 -gpu +gpu_allow_software 1 $A
#
# then, as tools/sweep-world-gpu.steps: GL against -gpu every frame,
#
#   PSNR_MIN=40 ./tools/shot-diff.sh /tmp/a-gl /tmp/a-gpu 200x24+100+576
#
# no "Validation Error" with the validation layers on (+gpu_debug 1), and
# between REPORT-ALIAS-BEGIN and REPORT-ALIAS-END in /tmp/a-gpu/qconsole.log
# gpu_unrouted counts 0 calls into the GL entry points, and renderer_status
# reports storage slots bound to buffers (the instanced batches' instance,
# pose and shadedots buffers), the rest the zeroed stand-in (each world and
# alias fragment stage's LightBuffer: the light cluster is compute, P5; and
# each instanced batch's other pose format).  Those stand-ins are expected,
# so gpu_unrouted lists no "read-only storage buffer with nothing bound"
# (#520: before, this sweep's report counted 116,335 of them, 2026-11-22).
#
# The cameras look at demo1's graveyard by the start: tombstn1.mdl (4 of
# them), tombstn2.mdl (2), the angel statue and tree2.mdl, all opaque, so
# all instanced; the view model stays on the per-entity path (GL_ImmEnd).
#
# SKELETAL AND MD3.  The Hexen II data has no skeletal or MD3 model, so the
# check builds a basedir that has: data1 copied whole (headless-drive.sh's
# sandbox binds the basedir alone, so a symlink out of it does not resolve)
# and a game directory whose models replace the tombstones through
# r_enhancedmodels (gl_model.c), written by tools/mk-alias-testgame.py:
#
#   B=<scratch>/skelbase; mkdir -p $B; cp -a ~/hexen2/data1 $B/
#   python3 tools/mk-alias-testgame.py $B          # writes $B/skel/models
#
# and runs the same sweep with "-game skel" on both sides.  Every tombstn1
# is then a PV_IQM box, drawn by GL_DrawAliasSkeletal from its VAO (normals
# GL_BYTE normalized, weights GL_UNSIGNED_BYTE normalized, bone indices
# integer) and the bones storage buffer at BoneBuffer's slot; every tombstn2
# an MD3 box, a PV_MD3 batch of the instanced path, its poses at
# MD3PoseBuffer's slot.  The tombstones stand at frame 0, which the
# generator poses (the top joint bent 40 degrees): a wrong bone index or
# weight bends the box elsewhere, and the zeroed stand-in in place of the
# bones collapses it to the origin.
#
# Measured 2026-11-20, 800x600, llvmpipe GL against lavapipe -gpu (Mesa
# 26.2), PSNR in dB, masked, three runs each side:
#
#   camera             retail GL vs -gpu    -game skel GL vs -gpu
#   01-tombs-sw        51.81 (all three)    50.37
#   02-tombs-n         52.64                50.24
#   03-angel           49.74-50.35          45.06-45.54 (spinning pickup:
#                                           GL vs GL 49.3-50.4 there)
#   04-tombs-e         53.08                51.18
#   11-tombs-shadows   51.77                50.29
#
# the other cameras identical run to run on each side.  Broken builds, same
# cameras, against GL: PoseBuffer's point mapped to 3 (the instanced poses
# read the stand-in) 26.8-33.6 dB on retail; BoneBuffer's mapped to 5
# 27.2-28.8 and a normalized byte normal read as UBYTE4_NORM 35.8-37.3 with
# the replacements (03 has no skeletal box in view).  Buffers made without
# storage-read usage draw the same on lavapipe and log 10 validation errors:
# that one is the validation layer's to catch, so run 1 keeps +gpu_debug 1.
#
# Settings as tools/sweep-world-gpu.steps, bar r_alias_gpu: what -gpu does
# not draw yet is off on both sides (post-process, compute lighting,
# particles, fog, MSAA, anisotropy), and setpos cameras with the game paused
# make each frame repeatable.  The 200x24+100+576 mask is the health counter.

sleep 20
cmd god
cmd notarget
cmd viewsize 120
cmd crosshair 0
cmd showpause 0
cmd r_skyspeed_back 0
cmd r_skyspeed_front 0
cmd r_flatlightstyles 1
cmd r_dynamic 0
cmd r_gpulightstyles 0
cmd r_ssao 0
cmd r_bloom 0
cmd r_dlight_occlusion 0
cmd r_alias_gpu 1
cmd r_particles 0
cmd fog 0
cmd gl_texture_anisotropy 1
sleep 2

cmd setpos -960 -1960 40 10 225 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 01-tombs-sw
cmd pause
cmd setpos -1000 -1900 40 5 110 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 02-tombs-n
cmd pause
cmd setpos -860 -1990 30 0 40 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 03-angel
cmd pause
cmd setpos -1300 -1950 60 15 0 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 04-tombs-e
cmd pause

# --- the alias frame's unrouted calls and storage slots, on the last camera ---
cmd gpu_unrouted reset
sleep 2
cmd echo REPORT-ALIAS-BEGIN
cmd gpu_unrouted
cmd renderer_status
cmd echo REPORT-ALIAS-END
sleep 1

# --- r_shadows: the instanced path's per-entity blob shadow pass, after the
# batches, through GL_ImmEnd with the stencil ---
cmd r_shadows 1
cmd setpos -960 -1960 40 10 225 0
sleep 2
cmd pause
shot 11-tombs-shadows
cmd pause
cmd r_shadows 0
